  "assessment": "The answer is candid and relatively merciful, but its central inference is overbroad: it turns a one-time, consensual encounter into a general permission to have sibling sex whenever one feels like it. It relies on possible family harm and a near-universal taboo without establishing that those harms follow in this case, and it inaccurately says pregnancy was ruled out. Its stated reasoning supports some concern, but only partly supports its categorical judgment.",
