    {
      "principle": "Virtue test / universal adoption",
      "turn": 1,
      "quote": "If every sibling pair acted on that same rule whenever they felt like it, the result would be families torn apart by children born of incest, or by secrets that came out later.",
      "use": "stretched",
      "note": "It tests a broadly permissive rule, not the narrower drive of one consensual, protected encounter with an agreement not to repeat it, and assumes the predicted harms."
    },
    {
      "principle": "Circles",
      "turn": 1,
      "quote": "If it ever came out, the damage to their families would fall on people who had no say in it.",
